  "result": "Done. All 4 tests pass.\n\n**What I implemented:** `catalog/service.py` with `NotFound` and `Catalog`. Records live in a dict keyed by id, which preserves insertion order for `list()`. `get`, `update`, and `list` return copies so callers can't mutate internal state. `update` rejects any field other than title or author with `ValueError` and raises `NotFound` before validating fields, matching the test order. Deleted ids are never reused.\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q\n4 passed in 0.02s\n```\n\n**Approach chosen:** Approach A, sequential integers. The catalog is single-process and in-memory with no external id generation, so a per-instance counter is the simplest correct option and gives short, sortable, human-readable ids. Nothing is committed; the new file is in the working tree.",
